  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e81bb16ba40385c4bb6dac73ed24daa7, type: 3}
  m_Name: ModelCard
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SimuLean.Unity.SimuLeanModelCard
  displayName: "Reactions \u2014 a buffer that signals full and drained"
  description: 'Signals and reactions at their simplest: a buffer stops its source when it fills to 8 and resumes it when it drains to 2, so the buffer never holds more than 8.'
  author: SimuLean
  scenePath: Assets/Scenes/ReactionsDemo.unity
  copiedFrom: 
  created: 2026-11-09 12:00:00
  modified: 2026-11-09 12:00:00
  represents: 'Source (exponential, mean 4 s) -> Buffer (capacity 20) -> Machine (1 slot, constant 5 s) -> Sink: the machine is slower than the arrivals, so the buffer would grow. Reaction Buffer full: on the Buffer''s signal ItemEntered, when element.content >= 8, Stop the Source (Immediate). Reaction Buffer drained: on ItemExited, when element.content <= 2, Resume the Source (a resume of a running source does nothing). Both act at the next event (timing NextEvent).'
  kpis: 'out=Sink.input, bufMax=Buffer.content_max, bufAvg=Buffer.content_avg, util=Machine.utilization, stops=reaction:Buffer full.fired, resumes=reaction:Buffer drained.fired.

    Seeds 1..3, 1000 s: about 197 out, the buffer at most 8 (never 20) and 3.8 on average, the machine busy 0.99 of the time, about 10 stops (the drained reaction fires about 71 times, each time the buffer is at 2 or less on an exit).'
  parameters: 'The thresholds are in the reactions'' conditions (texts: element.content >= 8 / <= 2); reaction:Buffer full.reactionEnabled / reaction:Buffer drained.reactionEnabled (true / false: with both off the buffer fills to 20 and the source blocks); Source.interArrivalDistribution.exponentialRate (0.25 per s); Machine.delayStrategy.constantValue (5 s).'
  assumptions: 'A feature demo, not a real system: time unit s, horizon 1000 s, no warm-up, a fresh seed per run. While stopped the source creates nothing and holds the one item that came (arrivalsOnStop Hold; Pause / Lose are the alternatives). Reactions are the signal-based logic of Assets/Docs/Signals_And_Reactions.md; ChoiceLogicDemo and Workshop_Advanced use them in larger models.'
